2. DISTRIBUTION AND PACKAGING BOUNDARIES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2.1 Official Channel Integrity: Redistribution, re-uploading, mirroring, repackaging,
    or re-hosting of the Software (whether in source form, modified form, or compiled
    installers) on third-party platforms, download portals, or app stores without
    prior written consent from the Copyright Holder is strictly prohibited.

2.2 Distribution Channels: Official releases, installers, and updates shall be
    published exclusively through the official project repository and designated
    channels managed by the Copyright Holder.

    Explanatory Note: This boundary protects players from downloading unauthorized,
    tampered, or outdated builds containing potential security risks or malware,
    ensuring everyone receives authentic Pyra releases.


3. BACKEND INFRASTRUCTURE AND CATALOG GOVERNANCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.1 Scope of Backend Governance: The `backend/` directory—comprising serverless API
    handlers (`backend/api/catalog.ts`), production catalog metadata (`backend/api/catalog.json`),
    deployment manifests (`backend/vercel.json`), and related service code is governed
    under single-maintainer administration by the Copyright Holder.

3.2 Production Deployment Rights: The deployment, hosting, operation, and production
    management of the catalog API service are reserved exclusively to the Copyright
    Holder. Third parties may not host, operate, or deploy public instances of the
    Pyra backend API or catalog server.

3.3 Community Catalog Proposals: Community members are warmly encouraged to propose
    new game listings, metadata updates, or catalog enhancements by submitting Pull
    Requests to `backend/api/catalog.json` or opening Issue requests in the official
    repository.

    Explanatory Note: Maintaining a single production backend ensures game metadata
    accuracy, verified CDN download sources, and download safety for all users,
    preventing fragmented or malicious catalog servers while empowering the community
    to contribute new games via official PRs.


